	(text "ATtiny3216 at 10 MHz (internal 20 MHz / 2; 20 MHz needs 4.5 V). I2C target to the Pi at 0x30/0x31/0x32.\nKeep a pre-computed register snapshot so a read never stretches SCL (Broadcom BSC). 100 kHz.\nTri-state PC2/PC3 (hub EEPROM bus) whenever +3.3V is down - the MCU outlives it by design.\nALERT is open-drain in firmware; pull-up to PI3.3 so it exists only with a Pi (no back-power).\nDo not fuse PA0 to RESET: recovering UPDI needs a 12 V pulse."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "27c8a6f9-a368-535b-8154-e22a9f178310")
	)
	(text "TEST POINTS - link and resets"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 23 259 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "32fd2fcd-7669-502d-86a9-38b681327749")
	)
	(text "INTER-BOARD SIGNAL LINK, 9-way (power is a separate 4-way: different pin counts cannot be swapped).\nJ8 header (right edge) mates J9 socket (left edge) of the next board directly - no cable.\nThe invariant is physical position, not pin number. SPARE1/SPARE2 sit on USART0 (PB2/PB3) for an\nRS-485 migration if the single-ended link misbehaves. ~100 pF vs Pi 1.8k = ~150 ns rise (1 us limit)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170 190 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6619755e-5508-5c5e-a0ae-d4a0e83b0a65")
	)
	(text "BOARD IDENTITY - the only build difference. 10k pull-ups always fitted; 0R to GND per board:\n  board 1: ID1 fitted, ID0 fitted -> 0x30    board 2: ID1 fitted, ID0 omitted -> 0x31\n  board 3: ID1 omitted, ID0 fitted -> 0x32   (external pulls: identity is measurable with a meter)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170 110 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "79863086-433c-5f97-b178-cfe7d6a6236c")
	)
	(text "UPDI: GND in the centre. A reversed plug swaps\n+3V3 and UPDI but never the reference."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 85 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cbc41ed0-414d-5a0f-bf2a-4b0df76e87ee")
	)
	(text "RAIL MONITORING: ~2.0 V at nominal vs internal 2.5 V ref. 100 nF at each tap.\nSenses protected +24V, not +24V_RAW. JP2 selects 100 nF (default) or 22 uF on the 24 V tap:\nSHIP ON 100 nF - 22 uF x 3.9k = 86 ms averages away the dip the monitor exists to catch."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170 22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ff88af84-914a-5c8d-9716-53ae37030efd")
	)
